the virtual high street was created to  support  local businesses impacted by the  coronavirus pandemic  working in partnership with sudbury town  council baber district council wanted to  create a platform for businesses to come  together  and provide a space for customers to  find their favorite stores on one  digital platform  many businesses didn't have a digital  presence and the easy to use platform  meant they could upload products  and information quickly and easily  the virtual high street provides a door  into sudbury's high street  connecting retailers with existing and  new customers  it also allows businesses to upload  information about their store opening  click and collect or delivery options  product ranges  and more the virtual high street is part  of our wider ambition to support our  local high streets  and encourage people to shop local  the platform was built by a local  software developer who is based in one  of the region's growing tech hubs  innovation labs in stowe market  the virtual high street is just such an  amazing tool to find out  what sudbury has to offer from pubs and  cafes and restaurants to the library  you know if you're not one for internet  shopping then it's perfect just to see  what we've got and then maybe take a  trip  out and enjoy welcome to sudbury's  virtual high street  so i'm sarah and i'm from ducking boots  and um  we operate a shop like this one um  with outlets lots of small businesses  and we also operate the two pop-up  shop units out the front helping  businesses to connect with local  customers  starting any business is a really tricky  um decision to make the further we went  into renovating our little shop  the more it was becoming clear that a  lockdown was going to be  inevitable  spring summer stock had just arrived so  the shop was full of spring  summer i was a bit concerned that you  know i might get stuck with a load of  stock  during lockdown we set up a website so  we could start loading  the product online helping local people  in sudbury to discover  and shop local providing convenience  choice and flexibility discover  fantastic local businesses on your  doorstep  i've been looking online for quite a  long time and then thinking oh i won't  be able to do that  so i'm sure if i we can do it anyone can  do it  my message to the locals that have  supported us through the lock down and i  suppose supported all of the businesses  through sudbury is just thank you so  much it's meant the world to us it's  meant  the difference between opening our doors  at the end of all of this and not  opening our doors  after the lockdown it was it was busy it  was lovely  the market's amazing and i think the  market saw a lot of people through  lockdown it's a really beautiful little  market town  the virtual high street project has been  a real success  over 115 businesses have signed up  over the last six months almost 5 000  unique visitors have used the site over  70 percent of businesses involved  had no web presence before the virtual  high street  our ambition has always been to expand  the virtual high street beyond sudbury  but we have been blown away by how  quickly businesses have adopted the  technology  and how many residents are embracing  this online access to their local shops  we've now secured additional funding so  we can grow the project  and add more functionality to the site  next we will expand to other towns  including  stone market hadley needham market and i  including a program to help business  owners improve their digital skills  so that they can get the most out of  their online shop  by expanding the virtual high street to  all our key towns  we hope to support the growth of the  local economy  we estimate that if just 15 of the adult  population in baber and mid suffolk  made a one-off purchase of five pounds  on the virtual high street  we could generate an additional 109  500 pounds for our traders the future  looks brighter for our local businesses
 

